[Music]  here in this video we will take a look  at the most powerful monsters that  doctor strange has fought and defeated  there are nine of them which we have  included all of them have a monstrous  form that aren't human sized or  human-like of course there are other  powerful villains like doctor doom baron  model and casilius but in this list we  will only focus on the powerful demons  monsters and god-like entities that have  faced doctor strange in a way and lost  to him so let's get to it  starting with number 9 the undying ones  these are creatures who serve the being  called the nameless one and they are  demons from another dimension their  biggest advantage is their overwhelming  numbers however they are also very  dangerous in a one-on-one battle because  of their immense strength size and  resistance to most forms of conventional  attack the majority of these  lovecraftian creatures have mystical  abilities and can shapeshift as well the  undying ones invaded planet earth and  this forced doctor strange to form a  group called the defenders along with  namor from atlantis and the hulk and  they promptly defeated them and sent  them back to where they came from  and number eight we have despair he was  created 20 000 years ago by the dweller  in darkness out of terror by the sinking  of atlantis and lemuria he was given  some of the dweller's consciousness  and later gained his own self  autonomy or independence despair uses  illusions and hallucinations to instill  terror and despair in his victims he has  the ability to read the minds and  emotions in order to bring forth the  people's innermost fears he is a member  of the fear lords and in one instance he  made the dweller and a nightmare compete  in creating the great fear but this ends  up in terrorizing humans up to a point  where people's fear turned into despair  and then he became all the more powerful  from that and even though he became  stronger he was still defeated by doctor  strange in the end  at number 7 we have nightmare nightmare  is a class 3 demon the ruler of the  dream dimension and he is one who  influences the dreams of living beings  as they sleep feeding on humanity's  psychic energies in particular he uses  the energy he extracts from their  subconscious minds to keep himself alive  he actually requires it in order to  survive and without it he would perish  nightmare is extremely powerful in his  dimension and maybe even virtually  omnipotent within it but outside of it  he is less so doctor strange has been  able to cast spells and illusions to  defeat him in the waking world he is  another one of the fear lords along with  the dweller in darkness despair and  others  number six satanish  one of the many faces of evil satanish  is a class ii demon or hell lord who  rules his own hellish spirit realm  populated by damned souls enslaved  through bargains they struck with him  while alive satanish and the other hell  lords originated as fragments of a mass  of dark mystical energy remaining from  the battle between the demogorge and the  evil elder gods in his first appearance  in doctor strange issue number 174  satanish is revealed to be the hidden  master of lord necron  a powerful magician who bargained his  soul for more abilities  strange defeats necron and in turn  defeats the will and scheming plans of  satanish  at number 5 we have cathorn this monster  was an elder god and was the first  practitioner of black magic on earth  when all the other elder gods  degenerated into demons the demogorge  was unleashed to devour them gathorn  fearing it created a dark hole a book  filled with dark magic spells and then  disappeared into another pocket  dimension to escape the god either  catholic has always been more associated  with wanda maximov and her use of chaos  magic but on occasion has come into  contact with doctor strange their  battles have always involved strange  attempting to prevent catholics  re-emergence by breaking his possession  over models in doctor strange sorcerer  supreme issue 90 he saves victoria  monteci from giving birth to catharine  in secret empire issue 7 he breaks the  demon's hole over wanda maximoff  at number 4 we have the dweller in  darkness a member of the demonic cabal  known as the fear lords this  extra-dimensional behemoth has murky  origins and terrifying powers possibly  surviving from a previous universe the  dweller originates from the evarian  dimension the dweller appears in person  in doctor strange volume 2 issue 30  hoping to feed on strange and stranger's  love interest clear on their fear and  escape from the ancient spell binding  him in a mysterious dimension and  although he did manage to do that his  minions the shade trolls and later the  dreamweaver were all defeated by strange  so in a way strange did manage to fight  off the dweller's schemes but in the end  strange then succumbed to fear and a  dweller declared himself victorious so  this one is kind of like a one win and  one lose for strange here  at number three we have mephisto  he is a class 2 demon or hell lord  mephisto rules a fiery nether realm that  he refers to as hell or hades though  this is neither the biblical hell nor  pluto's olympian hades  or is it hades hades whatever mephisto  is one of the most powerful entities in  the marvel universe the comic book  equivalent of the devil and he's also  nearly godlike in his own dimension able  to even withstand an attack from  galactus the world devourer mephisto can  also reality shape-shift and cast  illusions on a scale that is near  impossible to comprehend  in doctor strange damnation  issue 1 mephisto and dr strange played a  game of blackjack for the souls of the  people of las vegas and fortunately  won the game  in another instance in the sinister war  storyline in amazing spider-man vol 5  the 204s strange and mephisto play  another fateful game of chance  one that ends with the freeing of harry  osborne's soul at number two we have  dormammu  we have come to bargain  dormammu is a primordial  interdimensional entity who wields  apocalyptic levels of supernatural power  and is the ruler of the dark dimension  described by marvel as one of the  greatest forces of evil in the universe  dormammu is one of the few villains who  can lay claim to being doctor strange's  arch enemy or maybe even more than that  as the creator and manipulator of  satanish he arguably dwelves the hell  lords in terms of sheer strength he also  held his own against agamotto who in dr  strange sorcerer supreme issue 43 holds  his own against galactus himself in the  mcu in doctor strange the movie strange  who is immensely overpowered by domamu  still manages to defeat him by using the  time stone to drop de marmo in a  never-ending loop forcing the monster to  leave the planet and does in a way being  defeated by strange  and number one schuma  this monster is the archetypal class 3  demon native to an extra dimensional  realm and a ruler of a hundred  dimensions  he is one of the old ones who came to  earth untold millions of years ago  ruling it and feasting on mankind's  ancestors in mighty avengers vol 2 issue  2 doctor strange is forced by ebony  moore to summon a tiny fragment of the  being known as shumagarath into  manhattan while being all powerful in  his own dimension  this small avatar of him was defeated by  strange however his entire being would  have been too powerful for anything to  stop him even jomamu and mephisto  acknowledged it as being more powerful  than them  anyway with that we come to the end of  this list so do hit that like button for  support subscribe as well to be a part  of the minecube family comment your own  list  but most of all smash the bell icon for  regular updates on new videos right here  on this channel till the next one take  care fam

